Install and update (Linux gaming PC, from Desktop Mode)
-------------------------------------------------------
Copy BLiNX2-@VERSION@-steamos.tar to the PC (USB stick, network share,
scp), unpack it (Dolphin: right-click > Extract > Extract archive here, or
`tar -xf BLiNX2-@VERSION@-steamos.tar`), open a terminal (Konsole) in the
unpacked BLiNX2-@VERSION@-steamos folder and run the installer. If
`./install.sh` says "permission denied" (an unpacker that dropped the
modes), run `bash install.sh` instead; the options are the same. The
unpacked folder can be deleted after the install.

  ./install.sh --steam      first time: installs to ~/Games/BLiNX2 and adds
                            "BLiNX2" to Steam (Steam must be open)
  ./install.sh              every later version: installs on top, keeps the
                            last 3 versions, saves untouched
  ./install.sh rollback     back to the previous version
  ./install.sh status       what is installed, where the saves are
  ./install.sh list         installed versions
  ./install.sh uninstall    removes the program; keeps hdd/, config/, logs/
  Options: --root DIR (default ~/Games/BLiNX2), --keep N (default 3),
           --import-saves DIR (copy an old save root into an empty hdd/).

Play from Game Mode: the shortcut is "BLiNX2" in your library. Leave
"Force the use of a specific Steam Play compatibility tool" OFF for it: the
launcher starts Proton itself (umu-run, GE-Proton).

The first launch creates the Wine prefix and takes 20-60 seconds with
nothing on screen. Later launches are quick. The prefix (~/Games/BLiNX2/prefix)
holds nothing of value and can be deleted; it is recreated.

If Steam was not open during the install, add the shortcut by hand:
Steam (Desktop Mode) > Games > Add a Non-Steam Game to My Library > Browse >
~/Games/BLiNX2/BLiNX2.

Controls
--------
A controller works as player 1. The keyboard works too, merged with a pad
on player 1, while the game window has the focus (RECOMP_KEYBOARD=0 in
config/launch.env turns it off):

  arrows          d-pad            Enter       START
  Z X A S         A B X Y          Backspace   BACK
  Q E             white, black     1 3         left, right trigger
  numpad 8/2/4/6  left stick       I/K/J/L     right stick
